tel; pavilion reservations are available May–September.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"nara-nature-park","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Nara Nature Park","title":"Nara Nature Park","subtitle":"US-41 corridor, east of campus","notes":"Choose a trail activity—hike, bike, ski, or snowshoe—and use the public chalet for its interpretive display.","short_summary":"A 100-acre park linked to Michigan Tech’s trail system.","evidence_claim":"The City describes Nara Nature Park as a 100-acre park two miles east of campus, linked to Michigan Tech trails for hiking, biking, skiing, and snowshoeing.","source_url":"https://www.cityofhoughton.com/nara-nature-park/","source_title":"Nara Nature Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The City states that the public chalet is open daily from 8 a.m. to 8 p.m.; trail conditions vary by season.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"nara-nature-trail-boardwalk","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Nara Nature Trail Boardwalk","title":"Nara Nature Trail Boardwalk","subtitle":"US-41 corridor at Nara Nature Park","notes":"Follow the elevated boardwalk along the Pilgrim River for benches, fishing sites, and water-access viewpoints.","short_summary":"A 4,500-foot elevated boardwalk tracing both banks of the Pilgrim River.","evidence_claim":"The City states that Nara Nature Trail Boardwalk is 4,500 feet long and includes fishing sites, benches, and kayak/canoe-launch access along the Pilgrim River.","source_url":"https://www.cityofhoughton.com/nara-nature-park/","source_title":"Nara Nature Park","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Use Nara Nature Park access and follow posted trail conditions.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_sa